  "worked_solution": "Since our cubic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-3))(x-0)(x-5) \\\\  & =2x(x+3)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x(x+3)(x-5) & =2x({x}^{2}-2x-15) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-15x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.$",
